--TEST--
`$uri->with`'s three non-removable components refuse a written `null`, so the type says which components can be cleared — `rule:core-classes/uri-removable-components`, `rule:core-api/a-nullable-field-omits-as-the-never-written-marker`
--FILE--
<?nvs
// A bag field is nullable exactly where the member has a removal to offer, so
// `scheme`, `host` and `path` are `string` and not `?string`: every reference
// has a path, clearing a host would silently clear the port and user-info
// beside it, and dropping a scheme is a conversion to a relative reference
// rather than a field's worth of behaviour.
var $u = Core\Uri::parse("https://example.com:8443/a");
echo $u->with({scheme: null})->toString(), "\n";
echo $u->with({host: null})->toString(), "\n";
echo $u->with({path: null})->toString(), "\n";
--EXPECT--

--EXPECTF-ERROR--
error[E0401]: expected `string`, found `null`
%A
error: aborting due to 3 errors
To read what a code means and how to fix it, run `nvs agent show <code>`.
